{"bank":"mathleague","grades":[6],"papers":[["mathleague/2004-05-g6",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2004-05 Grade 6 Contest","year":2005,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}],["mathleague/2012-13-g6",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2012-13 Grade 6 Contest","year":2013,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}],["mathleague/2018-19-g6",{"contest":"Math League","paper":"2018-19 Grade 6 Contest","year":2019,"url":"https://www.mathleague.com/index.php/annualcontestinformation/samplecontests"}]],"questions":[{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-01","type":"mc","prompt":"Of the following, which is between $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{3}{4}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0.2"},{"key":"B","text":"0.4"},{"key":"C","text":"0.6"},{"key":"D","text":"0.8"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-02","type":"mc","prompt":"A polygon *cannot* have $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ sides.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"21"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-03","type":"mc","prompt":"The brochure said, \"Watch your mail!\" I watched for 5 days less than 5 weeks. For how many days did I watch my mail?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"25"},{"key":"C","text":"30"},{"key":"D","text":"35"}],"answer":"C","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-04","type":"mc","prompt":"$1010 + 10\\,100 = 10 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"101"},{"key":"B","text":"1010"},{"key":"C","text":"1020"},{"key":"D","text":"1111"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-05","type":"mc","prompt":"A \\$5 roll of dimes has $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ more coins than a \\$10 roll of quarters.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"10"}],"answer":"D","topics":["money"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-06","type":"mc","prompt":"If 10% of a number is 100, then 100% of the same number is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"100"},{"key":"C","text":"110"},{"key":"D","text":"1000"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-07","type":"mc","prompt":"$(12+10+8+6+4+2) \\div (6+5+4+3+2+1) =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"60"},{"key":"B","text":"45"},{"key":"C","text":"6"},{"key":"D","text":"2"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","patterns"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-08","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following numbers is *twice* a multiple of 6?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"28"},{"key":"B","text":"30"},{"key":"C","text":"36"},{"key":"D","text":"42"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-09","type":"mc","prompt":"$54 \\div 3 = 3 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"54"},{"key":"D","text":"162"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-10","type":"mc","prompt":"A roll of wallpaper covers half the area of a square wall whose width is 4. The area of the part covered by this wallpaper is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"32"}],"answer":"B","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-11","type":"mc","prompt":"I need 12 pieces of fruit to make 3 glasses of juice. How many pieces of fruit do I need to make 10 glasses of juice?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"30"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"40"},{"key":"D","text":"120"}],"answer":"C","topics":["rates"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-12","type":"mc","prompt":"How many positive divisors of 100 are also multiples of 100?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"25"},{"key":"D","text":"100"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-13","type":"mc","prompt":"A *hendecagon* is an 11-sided polygon. What is the product of the number of sides of a hendecagon and of a square?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"44"},{"key":"B","text":"55"},{"key":"C","text":"66"},{"key":"D","text":"88"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-14","type":"mc","prompt":"(number of 0s in 1 thousand) : (number of 0s in 1 million) $=$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1:1"},{"key":"B","text":"1:2"},{"key":"C","text":"2:3"},{"key":"D","text":"4:7"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-15","type":"mc","prompt":"Every $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ number has at least one even prime factor.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"even"},{"key":"B","text":"odd"},{"key":"C","text":"prime"},{"key":"D","text":"whole"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-16","type":"mc","prompt":"If my pet runs 300 *cm*/sec. and your rocket flies 300 **m**/sec., then your rocket travels $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ times as fast as my pet.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"30 000"},{"key":"B","text":"10 000"},{"key":"C","text":"300"},{"key":"D","text":"100"}],"answer":"D","topics":["measurement","rates"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-17","type":"mc","prompt":"I multiply 2 integers. Their product is 32. Their sum *cannot* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"32"},{"key":"D","text":"33"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-18","type":"mc","prompt":"The average of 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, and 19 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15"},{"key":"B","text":"16"},{"key":"C","text":"19"},{"key":"D","text":"135"}],"answer":"A","topics":["statistics","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-19","type":"mc","prompt":"In a 3-act play, each act has 4 scenes. If 2 new characters are introduced in each scene, how many characters are in this play?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-20","type":"mc","prompt":"If $\\frac{3}{4}$ of our letters are bills, then the ratio of the number of bills to the number of other letters is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"7:1"},{"key":"B","text":"7:3"},{"key":"C","text":"3:1"},{"key":"D","text":"3:4"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-21","type":"mc","prompt":"$4 \\times 4^4 =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$4^4$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4^5$"},{"key":"C","text":"$14^4$"},{"key":"D","text":"$16^5$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-22","type":"mc","prompt":"Ten coins, each a penny, a nickel, or a dime, *cannot* total","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11¢"},{"key":"B","text":"19¢"},{"key":"C","text":"30¢"},{"key":"D","text":"31¢"}],"answer":"A","topics":["money","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-23","type":"mc","prompt":"The area of a square with integer side-lengths *could* be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"600"},{"key":"B","text":"700"},{"key":"C","text":"800"},{"key":"D","text":"900"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-24","type":"mc","prompt":"The total value of 75 nickels = the total value of $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ quarters.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"15"},{"key":"C","text":"25"},{"key":"D","text":"375"}],"answer":"B","topics":["money"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-25","type":"mc","prompt":"The following are all factors of $30 \\times 40 \\times 50$ *except*","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$1 \\times 3 \\times 5$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2 \\times 4 \\times 6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$5 \\times 7 \\times 9$"},{"key":"D","text":"$6 \\times 8 \\times 10$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-26","type":"mc","prompt":"Ten years ago, the sum of the ages of Ted and his twin brother Todd was 22. How old is Ted now?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"16"},{"key":"B","text":"21"},{"key":"C","text":"32"},{"key":"D","text":"42"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic","logic"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-27","type":"mc","prompt":"We have 6 tents for 18 campers. Each tent holds either 2 or 4 campers. Exactly how many of our tents hold 2?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"2"},{"key":"D","text":"1"}],"answer":"B","topics":["logic","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-28","type":"mc","prompt":"If 3 out of 5 dentists recommend sugarless gum, what percent *don't* recommend sugarless gum?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"20%"},{"key":"B","text":"30%"},{"key":"C","text":"40%"},{"key":"D","text":"60%"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-29","type":"mc","prompt":"The time $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ is 6 hours before 6 minutes after noon.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6:06 A.M."},{"key":"B","text":"6:06 P.M."},{"key":"C","text":"5:54 A.M."},{"key":"D","text":"5:54 P.M."}],"answer":"A","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":0,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-30","type":"mc","prompt":"The *digit-sum* of a whole number is the sum of its digits. How many whole numbers between 9 and 100 have an even digit-sum?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"45"},{"key":"B","text":"48"},{"key":"C","text":"50"},{"key":"D","text":"52"}],"answer":"A","topics":["counting","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-31","type":"mc","prompt":"At a rate of 80 km/hr., I can run $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ km in 18 minutes.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"24"},{"key":"C","text":"28"},{"key":"D","text":"30"}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-32","type":"mc","prompt":"$2^{2005} = 2^{2004} +$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"2004"},{"key":"D","text":"$2^{2004}$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","patterns"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-33","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of the digits of all positive primes less than 20 is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"77"},{"key":"B","text":"76"},{"key":"C","text":"41"},{"key":"D","text":"40"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-34","type":"mc","prompt":"If 2 pears weigh as much as 3 peaches, and 2 peaches weigh as much as 30 grapes, then $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ pears weigh as much as 90 grapes.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"A","topics":["rates","logic"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-35","type":"mc","prompt":"A square with a perimeter of 32 is split into 8 identical triangles, as shown. What is the sum of the areas of the 4 shaded triangles?","image":"qimages/mathleague/2004-05-g6/q35.webp","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"32"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-36","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of the 50 whole numbers $51, 52, \\ldots, 100$ is $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ greater than the sum of the 50 whole numbers $1, 2, \\ldots, 50$.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2000"},{"key":"B","text":"2500"},{"key":"C","text":"2550"},{"key":"D","text":"5000"}],"answer":"B","topics":["patterns","sequences-series"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":36},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-37","type":"mc","prompt":"Service without a smile costs twice as much as service with a smile. I spent \\$360 for 110 services, 100 with a smile, and 10 without a smile. Each service with a smile cost me","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"\\$3.00"},{"key":"B","text":"\\$3.15"},{"key":"C","text":"\\$3.30"},{"key":"D","text":"\\$3.45"}],"answer":"A","topics":["money","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":37},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-38","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the *total* number of times that the hour hand, minute hand and second hand go around a circular clock in 1 day?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"144"},{"key":"B","text":"1440"},{"key":"C","text":"1466"},{"key":"D","text":"86 400"}],"answer":"C","topics":["time-calendar","arithmetic"],"difficulty":3,"p":0,"n":38},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-39","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of 3 different primes is always divisible by exactly $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ different non-prime numbers greater than 1.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":3,"p":0,"n":39},{"id":"mathleague-2004-05-g6-40","type":"mc","prompt":"Every birthday of my life, I put as many pennies in a jar as my age in years. I now have \\$1.20 in the jar. How old am I?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"15"},{"key":"D","text":"20"}],"answer":"C","topics":["patterns","money"],"difficulty":2,"p":0,"n":40},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-01","type":"mc","prompt":"Pete the pilot flew 28 times last month. If 21 of his flights were at night, how many of his flights were not at night?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"7"},{"key":"B","text":"21"},{"key":"C","text":"28"},{"key":"D","text":"49"}],"answer":"A","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-02","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum $12 + 34 + 56$ equals each of the following *except*","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$46+56$"},{"key":"B","text":"$12+90$"},{"key":"C","text":"$34+68$"},{"key":"D","text":"$46+68$"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-03","type":"mc","prompt":"If I double the number of pens in my backpack and add 5, I get 23. How many pens do I have in my backpack?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9"},{"key":"B","text":"14"},{"key":"C","text":"36"},{"key":"D","text":"56"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-04","type":"mc","prompt":"$65 - (43 + 21) = (65 - 43) -$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"12"},{"key":"C","text":"21"},{"key":"D","text":"34"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-05","type":"mc","prompt":"The dime and quarter in my hand combined with the coins in my pocket total one dime less than \\$1. In my pocket is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"45¢"},{"key":"B","text":"55¢"},{"key":"C","text":"65¢"},{"key":"D","text":"75¢"}],"answer":"B","topics":["money"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-06","type":"mc","prompt":"Wednesday is five days after my party. On what day is my party?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Friday"},{"key":"B","text":"Sunday"},{"key":"C","text":"Monday"},{"key":"D","text":"Tuesday"}],"answer":"A","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-07","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following is the sum of two prime numbers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"17"},{"key":"C","text":"23"},{"key":"D","text":"31"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-08","type":"mc","prompt":"Each of my shoes weighs the same. If 2 of my shoes weigh 12 kg together, then the total weight of 12 of my shoes is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2 kg"},{"key":"B","text":"24 kg"},{"key":"C","text":"36 kg"},{"key":"D","text":"72 kg"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-09","type":"mc","prompt":"$25 \\times 25 = 5 \\times 5 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"10"},{"key":"D","text":"25"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-10","type":"mc","prompt":"(Six dozen) + (one dozen pairs) = $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ sets of three","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"48"},{"key":"B","text":"32"},{"key":"C","text":"24"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-11","type":"mc","prompt":"When Giggles the Clown correctly counts the dots on his costume in groups of 4, there are 3 left over. There could be $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ dots all together.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"31"},{"key":"B","text":"32"},{"key":"C","text":"33"},{"key":"D","text":"34"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-12","type":"mc","prompt":"What time is 420 minutes before 4 P.M.?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4:00 A.M."},{"key":"B","text":"7:00 A.M."},{"key":"C","text":"9:00 A.M."},{"key":"D","text":"11:40 A.M."}],"answer":"C","topics":["time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-13","type":"mc","prompt":"10 hundreds + 10 tens + 10 ones =","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"111"},{"key":"B","text":"1101"},{"key":"C","text":"1110"},{"key":"D","text":"101010"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-14","type":"mc","prompt":"Professor Quack had 7 more students this year than he had last year. If he had a total of 43 students in both years combined, how many students did he have this year?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"18"},{"key":"B","text":"25"},{"key":"C","text":"32"},{"key":"D","text":"36"}],"answer":"B","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-15","type":"mc","prompt":"All together, 27 trapezoids have the same number of sides as $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ triangles.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"16"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"27"},{"key":"D","text":"36"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-16","type":"mc","prompt":"In my garden, I have 6 roses for every 5 daisies, and those are the only flowers I have. If I have 66 flowers, how many of them are roses?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"22"},{"key":"C","text":"30"},{"key":"D","text":"36"}],"answer":"D","topics":["rates","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-17","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of two different odd numbers and an even number could be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"52"},{"key":"B","text":"61"},{"key":"C","text":"65"},{"key":"D","text":"77"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-18","type":"mc","prompt":"On a Sunday I put two rabbits in a cage. If the number of rabbits in the cage doubled every day, on what day did the cage first have more than 100 rabbits in it?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Thursday"},{"key":"B","text":"Friday"},{"key":"C","text":"Saturday"},{"key":"D","text":"Sunday"}],"answer":"C","topics":["patterns","time-calendar"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-19","type":"mc","prompt":"A pomegranate costs 4 times as much as a pawpaw. If one pomegranate costs 50¢ more than 2 pawpaws, then the pomegranate costs","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"50¢"},{"key":"B","text":"75¢"},{"key":"C","text":"\\$1"},{"key":"D","text":"\\$1.50"}],"answer":"C","topics":["algebra","money"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-20","type":"mc","prompt":"If I triple $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ and divide the result by 6, the quotient is 18.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"72"},{"key":"D","text":"108"}],"answer":"B","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-21","type":"mc","prompt":"$11 + 12 + 13 + 14 + 15 + 16 = 11 + 22 + 33 + 44 + 55 + 66 -$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"50"},{"key":"B","text":"100"},{"key":"C","text":"150"},{"key":"D","text":"200"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","patterns"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-22","type":"mc","prompt":"If Bob jumps 15 additional times, the total number of his jumps will be 3 times what it was 3 jumps ago. Bob has jumped $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ times all together.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"21"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}],"answer":"A","topics":["algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-23","type":"mc","prompt":"The total value of 10 nickels and 9 dimes equals the total value of 5 quarters and $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ pennies.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"14"},{"key":"D","text":"15"}],"answer":"D","topics":["money"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-24","type":"mc","prompt":"How many numbers between 1 and 100 are equal to 5 times an odd number?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"9"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"11"},{"key":"D","text":"19"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-25","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of the remainders of $123 \\div 4$, $234 \\div 5$, and $345 \\div 2$ is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"8"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-26","type":"mc","prompt":"If Marlon the mailman had sunny weather on exactly 12 of 30 days last month, on what percent of days was the weather *not* sunny?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"36%"},{"key":"B","text":"40%"},{"key":"C","text":"60%"},{"key":"D","text":"64%"}],"answer":"C","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-27","type":"mc","prompt":"Last month I spent \\$24 on magnets that cost 80¢ each, and this month I spent \\$24 on magnets that cost \\$1.20 each. The average cost per magnet was","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"\\$0.92"},{"key":"B","text":"\\$0.96"},{"key":"C","text":"\\$1.00"},{"key":"D","text":"\\$1.04"}],"answer":"B","topics":["money","statistics"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-28","type":"mc","prompt":"On a number line, $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ is the same distance from 1.75 as it is from 7.25.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2.75"},{"key":"B","text":"3.25"},{"key":"C","text":"3.75"},{"key":"D","text":"4.5"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":1,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-29","type":"mc","prompt":"$2^3 \\times 3^4 \\times 4^5 \\times 6^7 \\times 9^{10} =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2^{15} \\times 3^{21}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2^{20} \\times 3^{31}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2^{15} \\times 3^{40}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2^{105} \\times 3^{280}$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-30","type":"mc","prompt":"In a garage, the ratio of red cars to black cars is 8:5, and the ratio of black cars to white cars is 3:4. The minimum number of cars in the garage is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"20"},{"key":"B","text":"59"},{"key":"C","text":"74"},{"key":"D","text":"91"}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates","number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-31","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of 6 consecutive integers, the largest of which is 30, is equal to the sum of 10 consecutive integers, the largest of which is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"17"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"21"},{"key":"D","text":"26"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","sequences-series"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-32","type":"mc","prompt":"If a radius of a circle whose area is $36\\pi$ cm$^2$ equals the width of a rectangle, and the diameter of the circle is half the length of the rectangle, then the perimeter of the rectangle is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"60 cm"},{"key":"B","text":"90 cm"},{"key":"C","text":"144 cm"},{"key":"D","text":"172 cm"}],"answer":"A","topics":["geometry","measurement"],"difficulty":2,"p":1,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-33","type":"mc","prompt":"I wrote a list of consecutive positive integers beginning with 1. I then removed all multiples of 4, and I had 2345 integers left. What was the largest integer on my list after the numbers were removed?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3126"},{"key":"B","text":"3127"},{"key":"C","text":"3129"},{"key":"D","text":"3130"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-34","type":"mc","prompt":"At the start of my temporary job, I needed to load an average of 120 boxes a day in order to finish my job on time. At first I loaded 90 boxes a day. I then had 6 days left to load the remaining 1200 boxes. How many days did I have in all for this temporary job?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10"},{"key":"B","text":"16"},{"key":"C","text":"22"},{"key":"D","text":"26"}],"answer":"C","topics":["rates","algebra"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2012-13-g6-35","type":"mc","prompt":"Each day last week I counted 50% more leaves than I had counted the day before. If I counted 2430 leaves last Friday, how many had I counted the Sunday before that Friday?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"160"},{"key":"B","text":"240"},{"key":"C","text":"280"},{"key":"D","text":"320"}],"answer":"D","topics":["fractions-decimals","patterns"],"difficulty":3,"p":1,"n":35},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-01","type":"mc","prompt":"$2018 + 2019 = 20 + 18 + 20 + 19 +$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"2000"},{"key":"C","text":"3960"},{"key":"D","text":"4000"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":1},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-02","type":"mc","prompt":"If $\\frac13$ of my hats are red, and 36 are not red, I have $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ hats.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"18"},{"key":"B","text":"54"},{"key":"C","text":"72"},{"key":"D","text":"108"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":2},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-03","type":"mc","prompt":"The sum of the measures of the 2 smallest angles of a triangle *could be*","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"151 degrees"},{"key":"B","text":"135 degrees"},{"key":"C","text":"121 degrees"},{"key":"D","text":"61 degrees"}],"answer":"D","topics":["geometry"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":3},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-04","type":"mc","prompt":"$2018 = 20 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ $+ 18 \\times 1$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"10"},{"key":"C","text":"18"},{"key":"D","text":"100"}],"answer":"D","topics":["arithmetic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":4},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-05","type":"mc","prompt":"Every English letter appears in my 2018-letter password at least once. The letter A appears *at most* $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ times.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"77"},{"key":"B","text":"78"},{"key":"C","text":"1992"},{"key":"D","text":"1993"}],"answer":"D","topics":["logic","counting"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":5},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-06","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following is the product of 2 consecutive integers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"182"},{"key":"B","text":"195"},{"key":"C","text":"208"},{"key":"D","text":"221"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":6},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-07","type":"mc","prompt":"The least integer with a prime number of different prime factors is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"15"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":7},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-08","type":"mc","prompt":"I have 5 coins consisting of pennies, nickels, and dimes. If I have at least 1 of each type of coin, the least possible value of my 5 coins is","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5¢"},{"key":"B","text":"15¢"},{"key":"C","text":"16¢"},{"key":"D","text":"18¢"}],"answer":"D","topics":["money","logic"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":8},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-09","type":"mc","prompt":"Exactly $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ different 3-digit area codes can be made using only 2s and 3s, with at least one 2 and one 3 in each area code.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"4"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"9"},{"key":"D","text":"12"}],"answer":"B","topics":["counting"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":9},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-10","type":"mc","prompt":"How many multiples of 10 are factors of $10^2$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"4"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":10},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-11","type":"mc","prompt":"My team had to win a certain number of games to make it to the finals, and we won every 6th game we played. If my team qualified for the finals after our 96th game, how many wins did we need?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"16"},{"key":"C","text":"18"},{"key":"D","text":"90"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic","patterns"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":11},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-12","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the greatest common factor of $1 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times 9$ and $2 \\times 4 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times 10$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"3"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"15"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":12},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-13","type":"mc","prompt":"The expression $2^{400}$ is the product of exactly $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ sixteens.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"25"},{"key":"B","text":"50"},{"key":"C","text":"100"},{"key":"D","text":"200"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":13},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-14","type":"mc","prompt":"The 2nd act of a 3-act play is $\\frac13$ the length of the entire play. If the 1st act is twice as long as the 3rd, what fraction of the play is the 3rd act?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac19$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac29$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac39$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac49$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":14},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-15","type":"mc","prompt":"If I double my speed of 12 000 m/hr., my new speed will be","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"200 m/min."},{"key":"B","text":"400 m/min."},{"key":"C","text":"600 m/min."},{"key":"D","text":"2400 m/min."}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates","measurement"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":15},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-16","type":"mc","prompt":"Which of the following could be the perimeter of an equilateral triangle with integral side-lengths?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2017"},{"key":"B","text":"2018"},{"key":"C","text":"2019"},{"key":"D","text":"2020"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory","geometry"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":16},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-17","type":"mc","prompt":"The greatest of 10 consecutive positive integers is a prime number. What is the least possible sum of these integers?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"65"},{"key":"B","text":"77"},{"key":"C","text":"127"},{"key":"D","text":"129"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory","sequences-series"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":17},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-18","type":"mc","prompt":"One-fourth of Ed's balloons popped, with 2 balloons popping every 3 minutes for an hour. How many balloons did not pop?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"40"},{"key":"B","text":"80"},{"key":"C","text":"120"},{"key":"D","text":"160"}],"answer":"C","topics":["rates","fractions-decimals"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":18},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-19","type":"mc","prompt":"What is the greatest common factor of $6^8$ and $8^6$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2^2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4^4$"},{"key":"C","text":"$6^6$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8^8$"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":19},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-20","type":"mc","prompt":"The expression $100^{2018}$ can be written as the product of exactly $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$ prime numbers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$5 \\times 2018$"},{"key":"B","text":"$4 \\times 2018$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2 \\times 2018$"},{"key":"D","text":"2018"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":20},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-21","type":"mc","prompt":"How many integers have a square root greater than 15 and less than 16?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"1"},{"key":"C","text":"29"},{"key":"D","text":"30"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":21},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-22","type":"mc","prompt":"$\\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{81} = \\sqrt{9 + 81 + \\,?\\,}$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"0"},{"key":"B","text":"54"},{"key":"C","text":"90"},{"key":"D","text":"144"}],"answer":"B","topics":["arithmetic","algebra"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":22},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-23","type":"mc","prompt":"Each day for a month, Sully wakes up 5 minutes earlier than he did the day before. If Sully woke up at 6:50 a.m. on a Monday, on what day did he wake up at 6:20 a.m.?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Sunday"},{"key":"B","text":"Monday"},{"key":"C","text":"Tuesday"},{"key":"D","text":"Wednesday"}],"answer":"A","topics":["time-calendar","patterns"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":23},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-24","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of all factors of 21 equals $21 \\times$ $\\underline{\\;?\\;}$.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"21"}],"answer":"D","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":24},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-25","type":"mc","prompt":"$(1234 + 0 + 1234 + 1 + 1234 + 2 + 1234 + 3 + 1234 + 4) \\div 5 =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1234"},{"key":"B","text":"1234 + 1"},{"key":"C","text":"1234 + 2"},{"key":"D","text":"1234 + 3"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","statistics"],"difficulty":1,"p":2,"n":25},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-26","type":"mc","prompt":"On a number line, two different integers are each the same distance from my favorite integer and have a sum of 144. What is my favorite integer?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"31"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"48"},{"key":"D","text":"72"}],"answer":"D","topics":["algebra","arithmetic"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":26},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-27","type":"mc","prompt":"Last year I spent \\$180 for 80 pairs of shades. This year I spent \\$180 for 5 fewer pairs of the same shades. How much did the price per pair increase since I bought them last year?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"15¢"},{"key":"B","text":"72¢"},{"key":"C","text":"96¢"},{"key":"D","text":"120¢"}],"answer":"A","topics":["money","rates"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":27},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-28","type":"mc","prompt":"I drove at a constant speed of 60 km/hr. without stopping. At exactly 5:00 p.m. I had traveled 318 km. At what time did I start driving?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"10:42 a.m."},{"key":"B","text":"11:42 a.m."},{"key":"C","text":"12:42 p.m."},{"key":"D","text":"1:42 p.m."}],"answer":"B","topics":["rates","time-calendar"],"difficulty":2,"p":2,"n":28},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-29","type":"mc","prompt":"I added 3 of the numbers 11111, 22222, 33333, 44444, 55555, 66666, 77777, 88888, and 99999. My sum was one of these 9 numbers. When my sum was divided by 11, the remainder **could not** have been","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"6"},{"key":"C","text":"7"},{"key":"D","text":"8"}],"answer":"A","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":29},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-30","type":"mc","prompt":"I wrote the 101 integers from 1 to 101 in order on paper. If I wrote 101 digits per line, what was the sum of the last 4 digits on the first line?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"11"},{"key":"B","text":"17"},{"key":"C","text":"19"},{"key":"D","text":"21"}],"answer":"C","topics":["counting","patterns"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":30},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-31","type":"mc","prompt":"The product of all the factors of an integer greater than 1 equals the cube of that integer. What is the least integer for which this is true?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"24"},{"key":"B","text":"18"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"8"}],"answer":"C","topics":["number-theory"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":31},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-32","type":"mc","prompt":"On our last history test, at least one student scored each of the grades A, B, C, D, and F. If 8 got an A, 15 got a C or higher, 10 got a B or lower, and only one student got a D, how many students got an F?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"1"},{"key":"B","text":"2"},{"key":"C","text":"3"},{"key":"D","text":"5"}],"answer":"B","topics":["logic","arithmetic"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":32},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-33","type":"mc","prompt":"$(2^2 \\times 2^4 \\times 2^6 \\times \\ldots \\times 2^{98} \\times 2^{100}) \\div (2^1 \\times 2^3 \\times 2^5 \\times \\ldots \\times 2^{97} \\times 2^{99}) =$","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"$2^{49}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2^{50}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2^{100}$"}],"answer":"C","topics":["arithmetic","sequences-series"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":33},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-34","type":"mc","prompt":"Starting at 1:00 p.m., a ball was rolled in each of two lanes. A ball was rolled once every 15 seconds in one lane and once every 18 seconds in the other. By 1:44 p.m., how many times had balls been rolled at the same time in both lanes?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"29"},{"key":"B","text":"30"},{"key":"C","text":"40"},{"key":"D","text":"44"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","time-calendar"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":34},{"id":"mathleague-2018-19-g6-35","type":"mc","prompt":"I counted backwards out loud from 2018 by ones. When I said my 50th multiple of 8, how many numbers had I counted?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"252"},{"key":"B","text":"395"},{"key":"C","text":"400"},{"key":"D","text":"1618"}],"answer":"B","topics":["number-theory","counting"],"difficulty":3,"p":2,"n":35}]}